{"id": "unknown-2026-08-25-004", "date": "2026-08-25", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.25, "keywords": ["[否定]outperform", "improve"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "New temperature model improves floating PV performance predictions", "content": "<p>Researchers in Malaysia have developed a simplified operating cell temperature model for floating photovoltaic (FPV) systems that incorporates water temperature while remaining compatible with existing nominal operating cell temperature (NOCT) models. The FPV-NOCT model outperformed the standard NOCT approach in validation datasets from Brazil and California, achieving up to 92.3% prediction accuracy.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/25/new-temperature-model-improv", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/25/new-temperature-model-improves-floating-pv-performance-predictions/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-25-005", "date": "2026-08-25", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "TCL Electronics weighs spinoff of $2.7 billion PV business", "content": "<p>TCL Electronics Holdings says t is weighing a separate stock exchange listing for its PV business, which generated HKD 21.06 billion ($2.7 billion) in revenue in 2025.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/25/tcl-electronics-weighs-spin-off-of-2-7-billion-pv-business/\">TCL Electronics weighs spinoff of $2.7 billion PV business</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/25/tcl-electronics-weighs-spin-off-of-2-7-billion-pv-business/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-25-006", "date": "2026-08-25", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -1.0, "keywords": ["loss"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.65, "reasons": ["情緒極端"]}, "title": "Semi-transparent PV reduces greenhouse temperatures by up to 5 C", "content": "<p>Semi-transparent photovoltaic modules can reduce greenhouse temperatures by up to 5 C while cutting water losses by more than 60%, according to research from the University of Jaén. The study compared CdTe and amorphous silicon technologies, highlighting the role of spectral transmission in balancing solar generation with crop requirements.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/25/la-fotovoltaica-semitransparente-reduce-hasta-cinco-grados-la-temperatura-en-invernaderos-", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/25/la-fotovoltaica-semitransparente-reduce-hasta-cinco-grados-la-temperatura-en-invernaderos-segun-la-uja/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-25-007", "date": "2026-08-25", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "UK approves 400 MW solar project with 600 MW co-located battery", "content": "<p>Beacon Fen Energy Park secured planning consent from the UK government. The development consent order means construction of the 400 MW solar, 600 MW battery energy storage system (BESS) can begin. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/25/uk-approves-400-mw-solar-project-with-600-mw-co-located-battery/\">UK approves 400 MW solar project with 600 MW co-located battery</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/25/uk-approves-400-mw-solar-project-with-600-mw-co-located-battery/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-25-008", "date": "2026-08-25", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Saudi Arabia awards $1.16 billion for 8 GWh of battery storage", "content": "<p>The Saudi Power Procurement Company (SPPC) has finalized four 15-year storage service agreements with two consortiums led by ACWA Power and Engie. The 2 GW/8 GWh portfolio marks the first phase of the Kingdom’s massive battery storage procurement program. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/25/saudi-arabia-awards-1-16-billion-for-8-gwh-of-battery-storage/\">Saudi Arabia awards $1.16 billion for 8 GWh of battery storage</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-mag", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/25/saudi-arabia-awards-1-16-billion-for-8-gwh-of-battery-storage/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-08-25-009", "date": "2026-08-25", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "40 GW project pipeline has Australia’s energy transition on track", "content": "<p>A pipeline of about 40 GW of grid-scale renewable generation and energy storage has Australia on track to maintain electricity reliability as ageing coal-fired power stations retire but the market operator warns the transition depends on these projects being delivered, not just announced.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/25/40-gw-project-pipeline-has-australias-energy-transition-on-track/\">40 GW project pipeline has Australia’s energy transition on track</a> appear", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/25/40-gw-project-pipeline-has-australias-energy-transition-on-track/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "enphase-2026-08-25-010", "date": "2026-08-25", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 35, "weekday": "Tue"}, "entities": {"companies": ["enphase"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Enphase enters commercial battery storage market, announces IQ Battery C80", "content": "<p>Enphase Energy has opened U.S. pre-orders for its IQ Battery C80, a fully integrated, AC-coupled commercial energy storage system designed to scale up to multi-megawatt-hour deployments.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/25/enphase-enters-commercial-battery-storage-market-announces-iq-battery-c80/\">Enphase enters commercial battery storage market, announces IQ Battery C80</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/08/25/enphase-enters-commercial-battery-storage-market-announces-iq-battery-c80/", "type": "rss"}]}
